Package: phenoscapR
Title: Read, Analyse, and Visualise Single-Cell Spatial Biology Data
Version: 0.1.1.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("R.", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742")),
    person("Hanno", "Witte", role = c("aut", "cph")))
Description: Tools for importing, processing, analysing, and visualising
    single-cell spatial biology data from multiplexed imaging platforms.
    Supports cell-table quality control, marker normalisation, phenotype
    summaries, spatial neighbourhood statistics, and explicit sample and
    coordinate-frame registries. Patient-level inference enumerates label
    allocations for declared contrasts and retains unavailable hypotheses
    when adjusting for multiple testing. Grouped summaries expose missingness,
    eligibility, and denominator provenance. Optional canonical cell-table
    import uses 'cellspecR' <https://github.com/CTTIR/cellspecR>; optional
    Self-Organising Nebulous Growths embeddings use 'songR'
    <https://github.com/CTTIR/songR>. Both optional packages are available
    from <https://cttir.r-universe.dev>.
